# scripts/check-design.js carried two literal NUL bytes inside
# maskNonColourHashes — the masking literal was "\0".repeat(...) rather than
# " ".repeat(...). Functionally identical (NUL is not a hex character and the
# length is preserved, so line numbers stayed correct), but git and GitHub both
# classify a file containing NUL as binary, and every diff of it for five
# commits rendered as "Bin 16615 -> 22629 bytes" instead of a patch.
#
# The bytes are gone as of #125. This declaration makes the classification
# explicit rather than leaving it to heuristics, so a checker can never again
# become unreviewable by accident — which matters most for exactly the files
# that enforce the rules.
*.js    text diff
*.css   text diff
*.html  text diff
*.md    text diff
*.toml  text diff
*.json  text diff
*.sh    text diff eol=lf
*.rs    text diff

*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
